00\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000The Arts Commission meeting was held on Wednesday, September 18, 2019 in Community Room A located on the first floor of City Hall. Commissioner Perryman-Banks called the meeting to order at 6:30 p.m. followed by the flag salute. \r\rRoll Call\r\rPresent\rCommissioner Jacques Lesure, Commissioner at Large \rCommissioner Onna Erlich-Bell, District 2\rCommissioner Phyllis Battle, District 3\rCommissioner Vicki Perryman-Banks, District 4\rHelen Lessick, Public Art Consultant\rStephanie Maldonado, Senior Management Assistant \rAbsent\rSabrina Barnes, Director Parks, Recreation and Community Services Department\rCommissioner Aletha Metcalf, District 1\r\r District 2 Commissioner Onna Erlich-Bell was introduced to the Arts Commission by Ms. Helen Lessick. Mrs. Erlich-Bell is a longtime Inglewood resident and business owner. She is a wife and mother and holds a degree in Fine Art. Mrs. Bell is excited to be a Commissioner and to aid in shaping Inglewood through the Arts. Commissioner Lesure reintroduced himself as well. \r\rPublic Comments\r\rNone\r\rApproval of the Minutes\r\rCommissioner Lesure made a motion to approve the minutes from August 21, 2019. Commissioner Battle seconded and the minutes were approved as follows: \r \r Ayes: Commissioners Elrich-Bell, Battle, Lesure and Banks \r Nays: None\r\rStaff Reports\r\rHelen Lessick presented a staff report recommending the Arts Commission recommend approval of artists Dr. Dawn Norfleet with Kevin Deane as the finalist team for the IGAPP 2019: Music Composition and Performance commission, a contract for services in the amount of $12,000/ (Public Art Fund). There were two semi-finalists who were paid a $1,000 for a musical sketch, a narrative and a notional budget. There was an online panel that met and reviewed the entries. They unanimously recommended Dr. Dawn Norfleet and Kevin Deane. The Commissioners were given a copy of the proposal titled �The Home of Champions� and given details about the winning musical sketch. Ms. Lessick played the musical sketch for the Commissioners and stated that the intention is to take you on a musical journey. After the sketch was played Rochelle Williams (an Inglewood Art�s activist) spoke on the panel process. Ms. Williams stated that the process was good. The panelist did not know one another, not knowing was helpful in providing genuine output regarding the entries. Ms. Williams stated that she was ecstatic to be a part of the process. Commissioner Battle agreed with all of Ms. Williams statements and also stated that there were a lot of great artist to choose from but Dawn Norfleet stood out because of her originality and that she has captured different rhythms from diverse cultures. That sense of diversity is good for Inglewood being that we are mostly African American and Latino populated. Ms. Lessick stated that next is the steps for artist contracting. The goal is to have composed music that�s recorded in a studio and played at civic events. Commissioner Battle stated that she can�t wait to hear the project with live musicians and is very pleased with the process. Commissioner Lesure stated that it�s a nice piece that will be a great addition to live events. \r\rCommissioner Battle made a motion that the Commission recommend approval of artists Dawn Norfleet and Kevin Deane as the finalist team for the IGAPP 2019: Music Composition and Performance Commission in the amount of $12,000. Commissioner Lesure seconded and the recommendation was approved as follows: \r\rAyes: Commissioners Erlich-Bell, Battle, Perryman- Banks and Lesure \r Nays: None\r \rVerbal Reports Regarding the following Public Art Related Projects\r\rHelen Lessick stated that the Inglewood Open Studios normally has a formal request for support that comes in September but the Commission has not received one (as of yet). Helen Lessick provided a copy of the logo that the City of Inglewood�s Art Commission funded for Open Studios. Commissioner Lesure inquired the owner of the logo. Ms. Lessick stated that there was a three party contract with the City of Inglewood, the designer and Open Studios. The cost of the logo was $2,000. \r\rPublic Comment\r\rNone\r\rCommissioners� Comments\r \r None\r \rAnnouncements/ Calendar\r \rA new exhibition by Christopher Mercier at the South L.A. Contemporary Gallery, on Slauson Avenue. \rOn September 28, 2019, 7:00 p.m. at Morningside High school, Los Angeles Phil Harmonics will showcase one of their neighborhood concerts. The concert is free. You can get up to 6 free tickets by calling 310-419-3080. \rMike Fields live �A Fine Art Exhibition of Drawings of Jazz Greats� in the Parker Room. Mike Fields is an Ohio artist in residence in Los Angeles. Commissioner Lesure stated that Mr. Fields is an outstanding artist. \rThe next Art Commission meeting will be held at the City of Inglewood in Community Room A on October 16, 2019 at 6:30 p.m. \r\rWith no further business, the meeting was adjourned at 6:52 p.m.\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\bINGLEWOOD CALIFORNIA\r\rARTS COMMISSION\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00142\u0015\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0014\b\u0000\u0000(\b\u0000\u00001\b\u0000\u00002\b\u0000\u00003\b\u0000\u0000?\b\u0000\u0000E\b\u0000\u0000F\b\u0000\u0000b\b\u0000\u0000c\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000����ŷ�����n�`R��E�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\