\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000","minutes_text":"INGLEWOOD  CALIFORNIA\n\n  ARTS COMMISSION\n\nThe Arts Commission meeting was held on Wednesday, November 20, 2019 in Community Room A located on the\nfirst floor of City Hall. Commissioner Metcalf called the meeting to order at 6:30 p.m. followed by the flag salute.\n\nRoll Call\n\n  Present\n  Commissioner Jacques Lesure, Commissioner at Large\n  Commissioner Aletha Metcalf, District 1\n  Commissioner Onna Erlich-Bell, District 2\n  Commissioner Phyllis Battle, District 3\n  Commissioner Vicki Banks, District 4\n  Sabrina Barnes, Director, Parks, Recreation and Community Services Department\n  Helen Lessick, Public Art Consultant\n  Stephanie Maldonado, Senior Management Assistant\n\nPublic Comments\n\n  None\n\nApproval of the Minutes\n\n  Commissioner Banks made a motion to approve the minutes from September 18, 2019. Commissioner\nBattle seconded and the minutes were approved as follows:\n\n  Ayes: Commissioners Metcalf, Erlich-Bell, Lesure, Battle, and Banks\n  Nays: None\n\nPresentation\n\n  Helen Lessick gave the Commissioners a brief summary of the Percent for Arts Ordinance and their role as it\nrelates to it.\n\n  Sonia Yoon, Project Manager from NOWartLA.org conducted a preliminary public art discussion for the new\nbuilding that will be located at 923 Redondo Boulevard, across from the new Metro Station. It will be a mixed use\nresidential complex which will serve a population with a range of income. Fifty units of the complex will be for\nhomeless households who will receive assistance from Los Angeles County Health Services to help transition them\nfrom being homeless. The developers are looking to have artwork installed in the area of the tower on the east and\nsouth side of its face. A RFQ is being put together and is scheduled to go out on September 1 st. Construction at the\nsite is expected to start in December and be completed in 2021. Helen Lessick asked for the Commissioners to\nsubmit any artist recommendations they have. Commissioner Lesure asked what is the cross street and what is\ncurrently located at that site. Sonia Yoon stated the cross street is Long Street or West Boulevard. Commissioner\nLesure asked if that was the site of the Social Services building. Ms. Yoon stated yes.\n\n  1\n\f  INGLEWOOD  CALIFORNIA\n\n  ARTS COMMISSION\n\nVerbal Reports Regarding the following Public Art Related Projects\n\n  Helen Lessick gave a report and showed preliminary renderings of the IGAP 2020 MLK Day public art project\nwith artist Michele Asselin who has been working with 15 Inglewood youth. The youth have identified their mentors\nand taken photographs that are being transferred to banners. The banners will be displayed at the city’s 2020 MLK\nDay Festival on Saturday, January 18th. Commissioner Metcalf was very, very impressed and pleased with the\nproject. Commissioner Erlich-Bell asked if the project will be displayed elsewhere. Ms. Lessick stated the artist is\nproposing it be used for displayed somewhere for Black History month. We are looking and accepting any options or\nsuggestions.\n\nPublic Comments\n\n  Eileen Altman is an artist who recently graduated from USC and is currently working out of a studio in\nInglewood. Her studio is working on how to create a pipeline for black artists. She came by to observe the meeting\nalong with Mr. Avila who was there to support her.\n\n  Kimberly Lesure introduced herself and stated she is not only the wife of Commissioner Lesure, but an\neducator and resident of Inglewood interested to see how arts is progressing in Inglewood and how she can be a part\nof it.\n\nCommissioners’ Comments/Initiatives/Art Calendar\n\n  Commissioner Metcalf shared information on behalf of Yvette Bailey, Inglewood resident and UCLA alumni.\nShe is interested in sharing information on her organization called Peace, Love, Serve Project, a non-profit formed\nand interested in offering free courses in multimedia arts, animation, filmmaking, digital media geared towards kids\nand teens. Commissioner Metcalf stated she will invite Ms. Bailey to an upcoming meeting to share what she has to\noffer. Commissioner Lesure asked if Ms. Bailey had a website. Commissioner Metcalf stated she has a whole packet\nfor the Commission but that she wasn’t able to get in time but will get the info and have Helen share with everyone.\n\n  Helen Lessick stated this is the last meeting before the holidays. Meetings will resume on January 15, 2020.\n\nWith no further business, the meeting was adjourned at 6:58 p.m.\n\n  2","tries":1}